        "82a57e0b-fdb5-4a90-89b5-83287e228437": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "expand_by_default": false,
            "column_placement": "right",
            "heading": "Ingredients",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "content": "<p><strong>Black Bond: </strong>Acrylic resin, Aqua, CI 77266 (Carbon Black, D&C Black 2, Pigment Black 7)</p><p><strong>Clear Bond: </strong>Acrylic resin, Aqua</p><p><strong>Sealant: </strong>Acrylates/Ethylhexyl Acrylate Copolymer, Aqua, Propylene Glycol, Ethylhexylglycerin, Caprylyl, Glycol, Phenoxyethanol</p><p><strong>Oil Remover:</strong> Isododecane, Paraffinum Liquidum (Mineral Oil) - N.O.S. , Laureth-4 , Polysorbate 80 , Propylene Glycol, Phenoxyethanol, Ethylhexylglycerin</p>",
            "page_for_content": "",
            "custom_liquid": ""
          }
        },
        "accordion_LfRfJA": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "expand_by_default": false,
            "column_placement": "right",
            "heading": "How to apply",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "content": "<p><strong>Step 1 .</strong></p><p>Start the application with clean lashes. Curl them up so that all lashes are aligned.</p><p><strong>Step 2.</strong></p><p>Apply bond. Starting from the bottom of your own lash line apply the black mascara bond only halfway through the lash - avoid applying it all the way to the tip of the lashes like you would apply a regular mascara. Let it dry for 30 seconds and then apply a thin layer of the white bond to the lower part of the lashes and allow another 30seconds unit both the black and the white bonds get tacky.</p><p><strong>Step 3.</strong></p><p>Apply segments. With the tweezers, grab each segment and start applying the segments underneath your natural lash - get them as close to the lash line as possible but make sure they don’t touch your wet lash line and gently pull the segment upwards so that it will stick to the natural lash. With the other end of the tweezer gently push the clusters like this. Start from the inner corner of the eye and work outwards. If the outer segment is too wide and exceeds the corner of your eye, cut a few mm to fit your eye. To finish up, with the bottom tip of the tweezers press the segments towards your natural lash.</p><p><strong>Step 4.</strong></p><p>Seal and pinch. After the application wait 5min and apply the sealant with the tip of the brush under your lashes and allow 2min. Apply a small amount of sealant to the silicone parts of the pitchers and start pinching the lashes together starting from the inner corner of the eye and working outwards. Hold each pitch for 5 seconds.</p><p>WATCH TUTORIAL VIDEOS <a href=\"/pages/lashguide\" title=\"Lash Guide\">HERE</a></p>",
            "page_for_content": "",
            "custom_liquid": ""
          }
        },
